<title>CANADA: TrizecHahn Corp 1996 profits flat.</title>
<headline>TrizecHahn Corp 1996 profits flat.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			US$0.18		  US$0.18</p>
<p> Net			 24,700		   24,900</p>
<p> Revs		     338,600		  305,800</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: TrizecHahn said it presented the company's earnings on a pro forma basis to allow the users of the financial statement to assess the effects of the October 1996 merger of Horsham and Trizec into TrizecHahn and its subsequent business as a real estate development and operating company.</p>
<p>Previously, Trizec earnings were accounted for using the equity method, since Horsham (now TrizecHahn) had only a 48 percent investment in Trizec at the time.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
